// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`the crew in the conversation: Off > renders exactly what phase 2 rendered (no crew, no new words) 1`] = `"<main class="pane pane-foreman" data-pane="foreman" aria-label="Foreman"><div class="foreman-column"><header class="job-header"><div class="job-header-line"><span class="hue-dot" style="--job-hue: 107;" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 class="pane-title job-title">Job alpha</h2><div class="level-menu"><button type="button" class="chip level-chip" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" title="L2 Standard:  Up: L3 Large. Down: L1 Small. Click to change it.">L2 Standard</button></div><div class="job-menu"><button type="button" class="btn btn-quiet" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false" title="More things you can do with this job. ⌘K lists them too.">Job menu <span aria-hidden="true">▾</span></button></div></div><p class="job-facts muted"><span class="status status-running" data-group="running" title="Jobs the Foreman or its crew are working on right now.">Running</span><span title="The repository this job works in.">sample-repo</span><span class="num" title="The git branch this job builds on.">feat/sample</span><span class="job-policy" title="How much the Foreman may do without asking you (your global setting). Change it in the job menu.">Routine steps automatic</span></p></header><details class="how"><summary title="Show a short explanation of what this is and how it works.">How this works</summary><div class="how-body"><p>This is your conversation with the job’s Foreman, the Claude session that plans the work and runs the crew. Its briefs, questions and permission requests appear here for you to answer.</p><p>A brief opens in full while it waits for you and folds to its headline once you’ve answered; click a headline to open it again. Steps the Foreman took by itself are folded into one “routine steps” line.</p><p>When the Foreman waits for your decision, a <strong>gate card</strong> sits above the message box: its questions, what it decided on your behalf, and buttons that say what they do (Approve, Edit then approve, Revise, Other guidance). Its own “How this works” explains it.</p><p>When it wants to do something that isn’t routine, a card appears at the foot of the conversation: <strong>Allow once</strong>, <strong>Allow for this reply</strong> (when offered), <strong>Deny…</strong> with a note, or <strong>Always allow…</strong>, which saves a narrow rule you check first (listed in Settings). Questions come as a short form.</p><p>Write to the Foreman in the box at the foot. <strong>Send…</strong> shows exactly what it will receive before it goes. While it’s replying the button becomes <strong>Steer</strong>: your message joins the reply in progress and shows <em>Queued</em>, <em>Delivered</em>, then <em>Acted on</em>. <strong>Stop</strong> ends the reply; the job then waits for you. Each job keeps its own unsent draft in this browser.</p><p>How much asks you depends on the job’s permission setting (job menu, or Settings for all jobs). In <strong>Auto mode</strong> Claude Code’s safety model decides most steps; anything it blocks shows as a dim ⊘ line. Pushes, pull requests, rm -rf and migrations always ask, and org or force pushes are refused.</p><p>The <strong>level chip</strong> next to the title (L0 Tweak to L3 Large) says how much process the job gets; click it to see what runs and to change it. When the Foreman suggests a different level, or none is chosen yet, a level card in the conversation shows the rules’ and the Foreman’s suggestions side by side.</p><p>The <strong>Job menu</strong> marks the job done or dropped (nothing is deleted; <strong>Reopen</strong> brings it back), opens <strong>Notes and options</strong> (a drawer with the job’s notes for the Foreman and its options: level, stages, reviewers, testing, Fable, models), links to its classic page, and sets its own permission setting. <strong>⌘K</strong> (Ctrl+K) lists the same actions and more; press <strong>?</strong> for the keys.</p></div></details><section class="thread" aria-label="Conversation" aria-busy="false"><article class="thread-item brief-card is-answered" aria-label="Brief #1 · Investigate"><header class="brief-head"><button type="button" class="brief-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="brief-body-brief_briefs_1-investigate_md" title="Open the whole brief."><span class="brief-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▸</span><span class="brief-label">Brief #1 · Investigate</span><span class="brief-state">Answered</span><time class="thread-time num" datetime="2026-10-15T12:01:00.000Z" title="(full time)">59m</time></button><p class="brief-headline">Investigation done</p></header><div id="brief-body-brief_briefs_1-investigate_md" class="brief-body" hidden=""></div></article><details class="thread-item auto-fold"><summary title="Steps the Foreman took without asking, because your settings count them as routine. Open to see each one."><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> 3 routine steps done automatically<time class="thread-time num" datetime="2026-10-15T12:02:00.000Z" title="(full time)">58m</time></summary><ul class="auto-steps"><li><span>Start a helper: feature-investigator</span><span class="muted" title="Why this counted as routine."> · Starting a workflow worker is routine.</span></li><li><span>Read src/app.ts</span><span class="muted"> · feature-investigator</span><span class="muted" title="Why this counted as routine."> · Reading is routine.</span></li><li><span>Run git status</span></li></ul></details><p class="thread-item decision thread-line"><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">›</span> You allowed: Start a helper: feature-planner <time class="thread-time num" datetime="2026-10-15T12:05:00.000Z" title="(full time)">55m</time></p><p class="thread-item thread-line blocked-line by-auto" data-ask="blocked" title="Auto mode’s safety model refused this step by itself, so it never came to you. The Foreman was told and carries on without it."><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">⊘</span> Auto mode blocked: Run curl<span> · feature-implementer</span> · <code class="blocked-preview">curl example.com</code><span> · Downloads code.</span> <time class="thread-time num" datetime="2026-10-15T12:06:00.000Z" title="(full time)">54m</time></p><details class="thread-item auto-fold"><summary title="Steps the Foreman took without asking, because your settings count them as routine. Open to see each one."><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">✓</span> 3 routine steps done automatically<time class="thread-time num" datetime="2026-10-15T12:07:00.000Z" title="(full time)">53m</time></summary><ul class="auto-steps"><li><span>Start a helper: feature-review-errors</span></li><li><span>Start a helper: feature-review-db</span></li><li><span>Start a helper: general-purpose</span></li></ul></details><article class="thread-item brief-card" aria-label="Brief #2 · Review"><header class="brief-head"><button type="button" class="brief-toggle" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="brief-body-brief_briefs_2-review_md" title="Fold this brief back to its headline."><span class="brief-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span><span class="brief-label">Brief #2 · Review</span><time class="thread-time num" datetime="2026-10-15T12:20:00.000Z" title="(full time)">40m</time></button><p class="brief-headline">Review done</p></header><div id="brief-body-brief_briefs_2-review_md" class="brief-body"><div class="prose"><p>Two findings.</p></div></div></article><section class="pending-cards" aria-label="Waiting for you"><article class="thread-item perm-card" data-ask="permission" aria-label="Permission: Run npm install"><header class="perm-head"><p class="perm-who"><strong>feature-implementer</strong> wants to</p></header><h3 class="perm-headline">Run npm install</h3><div class="perm-actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" title="Let it do exactly this, one time. It asks again next time.">Allow once</button><button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" title="Say no. It skips this and carries on; you can tell it why.">Deny…</button></div></article></section><section class="thread-item live-row" aria-label="Foreman, replying now"><header class="thread-meta"><span class="who">Foreman</span><span class="typing" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span><span class="live-label" role="status">The Foreman is working</span></header><p class="live-action muted" title="The step the Foreman is on right now.">Sending work to feature-tester: Run checks</p><div class="live-text" title="The latest thing the Foreman wrote. The full reply appears here when it finishes."><span class="short-line">Checking the work.</span></div></section></section><section class="perm-card question-card gate-card" data-ask="question" aria-labelledby="_r_2_-head" aria-busy="false"><header class="gate-head"><p class="perm-who gate-meta"><span class="ask-label" title="The Foreman finished Review and waits for you before going on.">Brief 2 · Review</span><time class="thread-time" datetime="2026-10-15T12:20:00.000Z" title="Waiting for you since Oct 15, 2026, 5:20 AM.">waiting 40m</time></p><h3 class="perm-headline" id="_r_2_-head">Review done</h3><p class="muted gate-next" title="What the Foreman proposes to do once you approve.">Next, as proposed: Fix round</p><p class="muted gate-running" role="status">The Foreman is still working on a reply. Whatever you decide waits in the message box until it finishes.</p></header><fieldset class="question gate-question"><legend>1. Fix R-1 now?</legend><label class="answer-option" title="The Foreman recommends this answer; it’s picked for you. Pick another to change it."><input type="radio" value="a" checked="" name="_r_2_-q0"><span class="answer-label">a) Yes <span class="chip gate-rec">Recommended</span></span></label><label class="answer-option" title="Answer with this option."><input type="radio" value="b" name="_r_2_-q0"><span class="answer-label">b) No</span></label><div class="answer-option answer-other"><label class="answer-other-pick" title="Answer in your own words instead."><input type="radio" value="__other" name="_r_2_-q0"><span class="answer-label">Other…</span></label><input id="_r_2_-q0-other" class="text-input" aria-label="Your own answer to question 1" placeholder="Your own answer" title="Your answer in your own words. Typing here picks “Other…”." value=""></div></fieldset><div class="perm-actions gate-actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" title="Approve and start PR #1. Sends your answers, confirms the decisions you didn’t override, adds the chips’ lines, and says “At these versions”. The Foreman goes ahead with: Fix round.">Approve and start PR #1</button><button type="button" class="btn" title="See the whole reply exactly as the Foreman will receive it, edit it, then send it as your approval.">Edit, then approve</button><button type="button" class="btn" aria-expanded="false" title="Ask for changes: the Foreman stays in this stage and revises. Nothing is approved.">Revise with feedback</button><button type="button" class="btn" aria-expanded="false" title="Tell the Foreman something else: a question or guidance. Nothing is approved.">Other guidance</button><div class="job-menu gate-more"><button type="button" class="btn btn-quiet" aria-label="More actions" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" title="More: stop this job.">⋯</button></div></div><div class="gate-chips" role="group" aria-labelledby="_r_2_-chips"><span class="muted gate-chips-label" id="_r_2_-chips" title="These change only the next stage (or the level from the next stage on). Each adds one line to your reply.">Next step only (PR #1):</span><button type="button" class="btn gate-chip" aria-label="Skip next (PR #1)" aria-pressed="false" aria-disabled="true" title="PR #1 is outside the build workflow; this chip is for spec to review.">Skip next</button><button type="button" class="btn gate-chip" aria-label="Lighter (PR #1)" aria-pressed="false" aria-disabled="true" title="PR #1 is outside the build workflow; this chip is for spec to review.">Lighter</button><button type="button" class="btn gate-chip" aria-label="Heavier (PR #1)" aria-pressed="false" aria-disabled="true" title="PR #1 is outside the build workflow; this chip is for spec to review.">Heavier</button><button type="button" class="btn gate-chip" aria-label="Ask Fable (the PR)" aria-pressed="false" title="Fable takes a short second look at the PR, the first point it can look at from PR #1 on: added to the job’s Fable points. It costs more than Opus.">Ask Fable</button><button type="button" class="btn gate-chip" aria-label="I’ll do this part (PR #1)" aria-pressed="false" aria-disabled="true" title="PR #1 is outside the build workflow; this chip is for spec to review.">I’ll do this part</button><button type="button" class="btn gate-chip" aria-label="Raise the level to L3" aria-pressed="false" title="Raise this job to L3 from the next stage.">L↑</button><button type="button" class="btn gate-chip" aria-label="Lower the level to L1" aria-pressed="false" title="Lower this job to L1 from the next stage. An approval still owed is still asked for.">L↓</button></div><details class="how"><summary title="Show a short explanation of what this is and how it works.">How this works</summary><div class="how-body"><p>The Foreman has briefed you and waits for your decision. Nothing goes ahead, and nothing is ever approved for you, until you press one of these.</p><p><strong>Approve</strong> (its label says what it approves and what starts) sends your answers to the questions, confirms the decisions made on your behalf that you didn’t override, and names the versions you approved. <strong>Edit, then approve</strong> shows that reply in full so you can change the words first. <strong>Revise with feedback</strong> asks for changes: the Foreman stays in this stage. <strong>Other guidance</strong> sends a question or a note without approving; the card stays open. Approve needs an answer to every question (a recommended answer is picked for you). <strong>Approve, start after reset</strong> appears when Claude’s usage limit is reached: your approval waits and goes when it resets. <strong>Stop job</strong> is under ⋯ and asks you to type the job’s name.</p><p><strong>Override</strong> on an “Also decided” item marks it changed, with what it should be instead. The chips change <strong>only the next step</strong>: skip it, make it lighter or heavier, ask Fable for a second look, do it yourself, or move the level up or down from there. Each adds one line to your reply, shown under the chips, and saves the job’s options where there is one.</p><p>If the plan changes after the card appears, it greys out (“Plan changed since this was proposed”) so you can’t approve an old version. If the Foreman is still working, your reply waits in the message box until it finishes. A decision left 4 hours shows as parked.</p></div></details></section><section class="composer" aria-label="Message the Foreman"><label for="_r_0_" class="sr-only">Steer the reply in progress</label><textarea id="_r_0_" data-composer-input="true" class="text-area composer-input" rows="3" placeholder="Add something to the reply in progress…" title="The Foreman is replying. What you write here joins that reply: it reads it at its next step. ⌘/Ctrl+Enter to steer."></textarea><div class="composer-bar"><label class="composer-model" title="The model for your next message. The reply in progress keeps the one it started with."><span class="muted">Foreman model</span><select class="select" disabled=""><option value="claude-opus-5-5">claude-opus-5-5</option></select></label><span class="composer-spacer"></span><button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" title="End the Foreman’s reply now. Anything waiting for your answer is declined, your draft is kept, and the job waits for your next message.">Stop</button><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" disabled="" title="Add your message to the reply in progress. The Foreman reads it at its next step; its state shows on your message.">Steer</button></div></section></div></main>"`;
